menu "Voice Pipeline Capability Configuration"

config CLAW_CAP_VOICE_PIPELINE_ENABLED
    bool "Enable Voice Pipeline Capability"
    default n
    help
        Streaming speech-to-text and text-to-speech through the Volcengine
        (Doubao) voice services.

        Audio pins are NOT configured here. The capability binds to the
        board's `i2s_audio_in` (microphone) and `i2s_audio_out` (speaker)
        peripherals declared in board_peripherals.yaml, so it only works on
        boards that declare both, and it can never conflict with pins the
        board assigns to other peripherals.

if CLAW_CAP_VOICE_PIPELINE_ENABLED

config CLAW_CAP_VOICE_SPEAKER_SAMPLE_RATE
    int "Speaker playback sample rate (Hz)"
    default 24000
    help
        Must match the sample_rate_hz of the board's i2s_audio_out peripheral.
        The TTS service is asked to synthesize at exactly this rate so the
        firmware never has to resample.

config CLAW_CAP_VOICE_RECORD_DURATION_SEC
    int "Maximum capture duration per utterance (seconds)"
    default 8
    range 1 30
    help
        Upper bound on how long one voice_listen call keeps streaming audio to
        the recognizer before it forces the final packet. Audio is streamed as
        it is captured, so this does not size any buffer.

endif

endmenu
